                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] A Trip down memory lane of old flash games [/h1]\r\n\r\nI know Harvey's New Eyes wasnt made on Flash engine, but it sure has the spirit of those games! From the atmosphere, to story, to humour, it all gives off that Flash games vibe, which I find nostalgic, but its definitely not for everyone. If I had to describe it, its like a very PG version of Gretel & Hansel flash game and those old German fairy tales, with a mix of Tim Burton artstyle, and a bit of Psychonauts vibe? Althought not sure if this game is appropriate to show to kids, I mean something life threatening will happen to one of the characters in the story, and it will get censored heavily by pink paint so you wont actually see anything, but sometimes its preeeeeetty obvious what happened to said character, like its very on the noose about it with its humour.\r\n\r\n[h3] Humour is a trail mix of grimdark jokes with a little bit of everything else [/h3]\r\n\r\nWhich leads me to humour. It's kinda hit and miss for me. It has a lot of grimdark humour, especially in the first chapter, but the game kinda overuses it too much, so I start seeing it from mile away. There are other types of humour here, a lot of variety actually, including Stanley Parable style humour of narrator breaking 4th wall, or talking about protagonist, but again not all of it is funny, but at least one or two jokes will definitely make you smile.\r\n\r\n[h3] Best Daedalic p&c adventure game in terms of gameplay by far? [/h3]\r\n\r\nDevelopers genuinely cooked with this game in terms of item puzzles, and mini game traditional puzzles, THEYRE SO GOOD! I don't think I got stuck in this game for too long once, and almost all item solutions are logical, satisfying to figure out on your own, and won't take too long to solve. It also helps that characters you meet in game are well written, and some are even memorable. But mini game puzzles have to be the BEST part of the gameplay. All of them are so creative(well, besides maybe the totem canyon one), especially old man mneumonic puzzle and lying game. Lying game is legitimately a fantastic LOGIC puzzle for kids/teens, to showcase how logic actually works, it kinda makes me wish we had a whole p&c adventure game filled with these logic puzzles.\r\n\r\nONE FLAW of the gameplay is the Shaman bug. You have to look up guide in steam forums of this game, but basically if you talk to Gold Prospector too early(guy who tries to find gold) near bar, he will soft lock your game, and you'll likely wont be able to complete the game, and have to load previous save or worse. So do check out guide to avoid said bug.\r\n\r\nOverall, I think if you're a teen, or have nostalgia for old school flash games, you'll get a kick out of this game. And its also a strong recommendation for any p&c adventure connoseur trying to find unique games in this genre\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
